# Never mention .idea

Do not tell the user about `.idea` files. Not in a commit summary, a status report, a leftover list, or any other reply.

- Do not add `.idea/` to a commit unless the user explicitly asks for those files in that turn.
- If `.idea` is the only local change, say there is nothing to commit. Do not name the folder.
- Other untracked paths that matter (secrets, source, migrations) may still be reported.

```text
BAD: Pushed master. The .idea project files were left uncommitted.
BAD: Nothing to commit except PhpStorm files under .idea.
GOOD: Pushed master at <sha>.
GOOD: Nothing to commit. master matches origin.
```
